 "sourceFacts": {
  "method": "Pipeline of L4042 (HUD-counter shot frames, two-star template fit with the generic star template, lens scale from 1x cluster spacings) with a 30 px horizontal search; burst extents from close-up screenshots with the wall panel width in the 1x screenshot as the angular ruler. See ANALYSIS.md.",
  "control": {
   "description": "Lens magnification 4.975 (TR-7) and 4.997 (LMR27) over 1x; the LMR27 233 ms bands reproduce the 14 October values to 0.001 deg; the TR-7 5 and 10-round extents match the x0.8 law within their errors.",
   "passed": true
  },
  "points": [
   "TR-7 267 ms: Standard 0.214 deg, Lightened 0.158 against 0.226 / 0.161 at x0.8 (stored 0.146 / 0.089). The 200 ms Standard band is unusable (shot 2 under the reticle arc).",
   "TR-7 350 ms Standard 0.129 deg against 0.022 at x0.8 (tail); 483 to 650 ms on both suppressors 0.08 to 0.10 deg, at the estimator floor.",
   "LMR27 233 ms: 0.360 / 0.304 (14 Oct 0.360 / 0.304); 342 to 350 ms: Standard 0.191, Lightened 0.180 against 0.182 / 0.139 at x0.8: the Lightened advantage is absent in the tail, as on 14 October. 633 to 638 ms at the floor.",
   "TR-7 bursts: 5 rounds 3.30 / 3.32 deg, 10 rounds 6.02 / 5.98, 15 rounds 11.19 +- 0.19 / 9.58 +- 0.89 (Standard / Lightened) against 3.37 / 3.28, 6.47 / 6.13, 8.67 / 8.03 at x0.8.",
   "Fits over all 45 usable observations (three weapons, two days): stored chi2 1232, applied x0.8 477, best in the family 433; a 67 ms dead time fits the TR-7 alone (207) but not the AK-205 bursts. (Corrected 16 October: the first run counted the unusable TR-7 200 ms Standard band, adding about 40 to every variant; ranking unchanged. Found by L4044.)"
  ]
 },
 "inference": [
  "The 0.8 factor scale holds on all three recovery profiles measured. The site law fails in the same way everywhere: recovery of the last 10 to 20% of a kick is slower than the law, the Lightened operand does not act in that tail, and on the steep profile the climb keeps growing after 10 rounds where the law saturates. No residual survives beyond about 0.5 s."
 ],
 "unresolved": [
  "The mechanism of the tail; whether the late-burst excess appears on the 72 / 1.2 profile (15 weapons) and the 55 / 1.023 profile."
 ],
 "siteImpact": "None applied; the x0.8 scale stands. (The 15 October note that long bursts on the 104 / 1.459 profile were under-predicted by 25% was withdrawn on 16 October, L4045.)",
