    "id": "L4043",
    "title": "TR-7 and LMR27 captures: the 0.8 recovery scale holds on a third profile; the slow tail and the missing Lightened tail replicate; no residual beyond 0.5 s (the 15-round burst excess first reported here was a close-up ruler error, withdrawn by L4045)",
    "status": "finding",
    "summary": "TR-7 267 ms pairs sit at the x0.8 law on both suppressors and its 5 and 10-round bursts match it, but at 350 ms it keeps 0.129 deg where the law gives 0.022 and its 15-round bursts, re-measured from the 1x screenshots and a camera track (L4045), sit at 8.5 deg against 8.3. The LMR27 reproduces 14 October to 0.001 deg, Lightened again equal to Standard at 340 to 350 ms. All bands from 480 ms are at the estimator floor. Fits over 45 observations: stored 1232, x0.8 477, best 433.",
    "reopenWhen": "A capture on the 72 / 1.2 profile (M433 or similar) with 10, 15 and 20-round bursts, or a readable implementation of the recovery law."
   }
  ]
 },
 "superseded": {
  "date": "2026-10-16",
  "by": "L4045",
  "what": "The 15-round TR-7 burst extents (11.19 / 9.58 deg) and the late-burst-excess inference. The 20 m close-up ruler was wrong; 1x screenshots and a camera track give 8.5 / 7.6 deg against 8.32 / 7.62 for the x0.8 law. Pairs, 5 and 10-round bursts and the factor-scale, tail and Lightened-tail findings stand."
 }
